    "methods_description": "Participants listened to moral scenarios with intentional or accidental harm, then saw a final target word and indicated by button press whether it was congruent with the scenario (congruent half of the time). Intention and congruency were manipulated orthogonally, giving 4 within-subject conditions. For 20% of scenarios, a moral judgment question followed, and participants rated the punishment the agent deserved using a joystick.",
